WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.440
<b>Question 12: "A: Because the Question Is There!"</b>

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:10.860
<i>Looks like you've figured 
something out, Koshiyama.</i>

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.490
<i>But I'm confident in my answer.</i>

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:15.780
<i>The bigger question is...</i>

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:20.950
Now, all players, show your—

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.380
Just a moment.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.830
Let's see their answers one at a time.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:28.290
I'd like to hear how they arrived at them.

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:30.560
Then, we'll start with Shibata-san.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:42.060
<b>Friday</b>

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.240
Why did you think it was Friday?

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:39.100
Uh... It's not the 13th, but 
they all sounded ominous...

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.660
After all, there's a "Black Friday," isn't there?

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:44.240
Next, Mikuriya-kun.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:47.060
If his answer is correct, 
he'll hit 20 points.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:49.270
<b>Sun</b>

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:49.270
Sunday.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.650
Why do you say Sunday?

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:56.240
Basic arithmetic based 
on Zeller's congruence.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.130
H-H-How about that?

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:00.020
Mikuriya-kun made his guess of "Sunday"

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:01.990
using not history, but math!

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:05.120
<b>Sun</b>

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:05.120
It's not a guess. It's a fixed answer.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.380
Next is Koshiyama-kun.

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:11.800
<i>I arrived at my answer in my own way, too.</i>

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:13.440
Yes.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:18.720
I found my answer based on the 
third date given: May 15th, 1932.

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:21.990
That was the date of the coup d'état

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:24.100
known as the May 15th Incident,

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.310
when Prime Minister Inukai 
Tsuyoshi was assassinated...

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.810
<i>So he went with the May 15th Incident?</i>

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:32.940
But I didn't know which 
day of the week that was.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.280
I recalled all the details I'd read about,

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.200
but there was nothing that pointed
 to a specific day of the week.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:41.010
But then, I remembered.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:43.560
One book about the 
May 15th Incident said that

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:47.180
the Prime Minister's wife, 
when she learned of the incident,

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:49.800
rushed to his residence from the 
hotel where she'd been staying.

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:53.960
I read the book when I was in middle school,

00:01:54.830 --> 00:02:00.250
and I remember being surprised that 
the Imperial Hotel was around then.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.440
According to the information in the book,

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:07.760
his wife was attending a wedding 
ceremony being held at the hotel,

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.230
when she rushed back home.

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:10.860
Oh-ho?

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:12.980
In other words...

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:16.070
<b>Sun</b>

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:17.870
Because of the wedding,

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:19.540
that would make it a Sunday, right?

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:22.210
People didn't have 
Saturdays off work back then,

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:25.330
so most weddings would have taken 
place on Sundays or in the holidays.

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:28.830
<i>He got that not from the incident itself, 
but from the involvement of a third party?</i>

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.460
That's incredible, Koshiyama-kun! 
Great deduction!

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:34.290
Koshiyama-kun really is interesting.

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:37.290
If he keeps gaining more experience 
and getting used to things,

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.950
he could be great at quiz bowl.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:43.690
Next, Sonohara-kun.

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:45.740
You were the one who buzzed in.

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:47.070
Are you feeling confident?

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:50.480
Oh, I just trust my intuition!

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.090
Intuition, huh?

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:56.110
If you're wrong, you lose 
three points, and you're out.

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:58.550
Oh, that's right!

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:03.070
I don't have any particular 
reasoning behind it, but...

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:04.830
<i>Not.</i>

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:07.810
<i>They both said Sunday, didn't they?</i>

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:08.940
<i>In that case...</i>

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:12.960
<i>I've won this little game.</i>

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.420
<b>Sunday</b>

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:15.420
I also said Sunday.

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:19.730
Okay, we will now reveal the correct answer.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:23.950
The question was, "April 5th, 1722;

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:26.800
January 22nd, 1905;

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:29.730
and May 15th, 1932.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:31.730
All of these were, specifically, 
what day of the week?"

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:35.060
The correct answer is Sunday.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:40.550
The first date, April 5th, 1722,

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:42.080
was when Easter Island was discovered.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:47.080
It was so named because it was 
discovered on Easter Sunday.

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:48.290
Oh-ho...

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:52.430
And the second date was the Bloody Sunday 
massacre during the Russian Revolution.

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:53.540
Common knowledge, of course.

00:03:55.070 --> 00:03:58.430
Now, Sonohara-kun, since you 
answered correctly after buzzing,

00:03:58.430 --> 00:03:59.760
please distribute your three points.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:05.760
Akira-kun?

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:10.420
Isn't this a riot? Everything 
I've done to set this game up

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:13.510
has finally led to deciding 
who wins and who loses!

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:17.730
Is this game over? Or is there still a chance?

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:21.190
I don't really care whether I win or lose,

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:24.150
but all of you guys want a chance, right?

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:29.280
Just look! They all want me to subtract 
points from the guy at the top!

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:31.790
Get on with it. You're wasting our time.

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:39.000
You know, when I'm provoked, 
I just can't help responding.

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:41.630
Mikuriya Chisato, I'm subtracting...

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:43.720
three points from you!

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:48.600
Mikuriya-kun drops from 
nineteen to sixteen points!

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:52.470
<b>Mikuriya</b>

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:51.710
But he gets one point 
for his correct answer.

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:57.650
Way to go, Koshiyama! You took the lead!

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:01.610
Not using my own ability.

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:05.250
We've all been taking this seriously!

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:07.820
Why do you keep doing these 
mean-spirited things to interfere?!

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:10.930
What are you saying?

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:13.960
If I hadn't taken points 
from him, you would've lost.

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:16.590
Now, you have a chance! Isn't that good?

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:20.450
He thinks this is a joke!

00:05:20.450 --> 00:05:22.170
Throw him out of here!

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:25.340
Cut it out. Subtracting 
points is part of the rules.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:29.310
A true winner can win, 
no matter what the rules are.

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:32.430
Koshiyama!

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:37.600
If you let this chance slip by, 
I'll sneer at your failure.

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:41.520
There's his competitive spirit.

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:45.570
Nothing gets Mikuriya-kun down, does it?

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:48.160
I guess that's why he's so strong.

00:05:56.930 --> 00:05:58.040
Sonohara-kun, where are—

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:01.260
I'm done with this. I'm bored.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.250
I withdraw.

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:04.920
What?!

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:08.590
Hey! Sonohara!

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:11.980
It's just no fun.

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:14.410
Akira!

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:15.730
You can't, President!

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:18.310
I know you're worried about your brother,

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:22.020
but you should leave this to 
Sekigawata's club president.

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:28.070
Yes, you're right.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:32.450
I have to assume the responsibility of 
hosting the regular meet until it ends.

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:37.960
With Sonohara-kun's withdrawal, the meet 
will resume with the remaining five players.

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:39.960
<b>Squee</b>

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:41.960
<b>Uh...</b>

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:51.750
What do you want?

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:54.300
It's upsetting to hear you say you're bored

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:55.930
when you weren't even playing for real.

00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:58.430
Why can't you take the 
competition seriously?

00:07:01.090 --> 00:07:04.190
In any game, everyone's entitled 
to their own playing style, right?

00:07:04.890 --> 00:07:08.690
And quitting before the match 
is over is your "style"?

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:10.550
No, it's not.

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:14.340
You know, I'll gladly use infinite combos, 
bug exploits, or secret commands anytime,

00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:17.660
but I'll never use hack 
codes or no-disc patches.

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:19.870
What are you talking about?

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:22.910
In that last question, though...

00:07:22.910 --> 00:07:24.840
The day of the week? What about it?

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:30.230
I made the one-in-seven chance 
a two-in-seven chance.

00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:33.510
The kanji for "Sunday" and "Monday" 
look really similar, don't they?

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:40.100
I wrote it sloppily enough that it could 
be read as either Sunday or Monday.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:43.070
If the guys most likely to get 
it right said Sunday or Monday,

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:44.980
I could jump on board with them.

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:48.940
In other games, you'd call it 
a forbidden move, right?

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:51.650
So I'm done. I fouled out.

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:56.780
Sunday and Monday, huh? 
The kanji do look similar.

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:58.370
You really are cunning.

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:01.040
I get that a l—

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:06.500
Never do that again.

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:10.930
I-I won't! Are you nuts?

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:12.530
It's just quiz bowl... 
Just a stupid game!

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:14.300
You guys get way too worked up over it!

00:08:14.450 --> 00:08:15.910
Oh, is that right?

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:19.040
It looked to me like <i>you</i> were desperate 
to stir everyone up in there!

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:20.640
You don't have any friends, do you?!

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:22.480
Sh-Shut up!

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:27.040
In any case, maybe you can indirectly mess 
with people who take this seriously,

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:29.640
but you don't have the guts to 
face them head-on, do you?!

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:33.570
You're wrong! There's no one who'll 
face <i>me</i> head-on, that's all!

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:38.490
Hey! Let go!

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:41.470
What's your problem?! Let go of me!

00:08:41.470 --> 00:08:43.010
Just get in here.

00:08:43.010 --> 00:08:44.940
It's about to get even more interesting.

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:46.460
If you miss it, you'll regret it!

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:47.480
Huh?!

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:50.920
First, a wall slam, and now 
they're holding hands?

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:53.230
Oh, my God! Is this a new development?!

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:55.100
The president of Sekigawata's club...

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:57.760
...and President Sonohara's 
little brother are...

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:05.080
<i>If Mikuriya-kun buzzes in 
and answers correctly,</i>

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:06.890
<i>we'll both reach 20 points.</i>

00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:12.400
<i>I have to avoid getting into a sudden 
death fastest finger round with him.</i>

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:15.780
Three questions remain.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:18.030
<i>Koshiyama only needs one more point.</i>

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:20.240
<i>All he has to do is answer 
correctly, and he wins...</i>

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:21.550
Question.

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:23.950
Occurring in times of technological 
innovation roughly—

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:25.580
Yes!

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:28.240
<i>Innovation? Moore's law?</i>

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:30.530
<i>I don't know! I didn't hear 
enough of the question!</i>

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:32.130
<b>Kondratiev Waves</b>

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:33.990
The correct answer is Kondratiev waves.

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:36.880
<b>Q: Occurring in times of technological innovation roughly once 
every fifty years, the business cycle named for a Russian economist 
is known as "what" waves?  A: Kondratiev waves</b>

00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:37.280
Shibata-kun, Shibuya-kun, and 
Mikuriya-kun answered correctly.

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:39.010
Kondratiev Waves

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:41.260
With points added to each of their scores, 
the battle is growing quite chaotic.

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:41.260
Kondratiev Waves

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:45.730
<i>I need to get better at straight questions 
with early determining points.</i>

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:49.490
Now, Shibata-kun, how will you 
distribute your three points?

00:09:50.070 --> 00:09:51.080
Uh...

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:54.490
I'll subtract one point from 
Koshiyama-kun of Buzou.

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:55.460
Huh?!

00:09:56.320 --> 00:10:00.050
Well, you seem like you could answer 
correctly without buzzing in.

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:01.200
Don't be upset.

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:03.260
Oh... I'm not...

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:04.710
Thank you.

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:08.140
Don't thank him for taking
 a point away from you.

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:10.040
Huh? Oh, y-you're right...

00:10:11.180 --> 00:10:12.500
I kinda get it, though.

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:13.680
Question.

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:17.640
Used in dishes such as curry, its rich 
aroma earned the title "the spice—

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:21.010
Once again, Shibata-kun has buzzed in!

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:23.110
Where does everyone stand now?

00:10:23.110 --> 00:10:27.380
Shibata has 17, Mikuriya 
has 18, Koshiyama has 18.

00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:29.020
Oh, it's a close race.

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:31.650
<b>Turmeric</b>

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:31.650
Garam Masala

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:31.820
Too bad! Shibata-kun is incorrect!

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:35.150
<b>Q: Used in dishes such as curry, its rich aroma earned 
the title "the spice queen" for which spice?  A: Cardamom</b>

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:34.020
Ah, dammit!

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:36.960
That's a painful three-point 
loss for Shibata-kun!

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:42.450
Looks like it has come down to 
Mikuriya-kun and Koshiyama-kun, after all.

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:45.990
We've finally come to the 
last question, Onee-sama!

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:48.450
So we have, Yuki-san.

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:51.210
Will we put an end to what has 
become a free-for-all battle,

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:54.440
or will we go to sudden death? 
I can't wait to see what happens!

00:10:54.440 --> 00:10:57.420
And now for the final question 
that will decide their fate!

00:10:57.980 --> 00:11:02.190
<i>To finish this, I need to buzz in 
first and win the three points.</i>

00:11:02.190 --> 00:11:03.890
<i>If I answer wrong, I lose.</i>

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:05.770
<i>We're dead level.</i>

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:07.100
<i>It's now a head-to-head!</i>

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:08.600
Question.

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:10.850
Now a destination for Christian pilgrimages,

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:12.600
Jesus Christ's crucif—

00:11:18.100 --> 00:11:19.110
He got it!

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:22.320
<i>He's rushing! She didn't get 
to the determining point yet!</i>

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:23.920
<i>I buzzed too soon!</i>

00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:27.340
<i>But I had a feeling Mikuriya-kun 
would beat me to it.</i>

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:30.460
<i>I'll just have to work it out now!</i>

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.000
<b>That's incorrect!</b>

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:33.000
Incorrect

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:34.170
<b>It's over...</b>

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:38.760
Buzou's Koshiyama-kun buzzed in!

00:11:39.060 --> 00:11:41.020
<i>Christian pilgrimage sites...</i>

00:11:41.020 --> 00:11:42.510
<i>Christ and the crucifix...</i>

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:44.720
<i>What answer can I come up 
with out of those things?</i>

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:48.470
It's the last question, 
and your sister's smart.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:50.430
There must be more to 
this than meets the eye.

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:56.730
<i>If it's a Christian pilgrimage site, then 
it must be one of their holy places.</i>

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:59.360
<i>How do I narrow it down 
from the various possibilities?</i>

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:00.650
This was one of the classics

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:03.570
<b>The Hill of Golgotha</b>

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:03.360
that Sasajima-senpai gave us 
to prepare for the meet, but...

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:05.910
That's the perfect difficulty 
level for this round.

00:12:06.220 --> 00:12:09.550
<i>It has to be a difficulty level that 
warrants its place in the third round.</i>

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:14.870
<i>Maybe it's the place where Christ prayed 
the night before he was crucified?</i>

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:15.250
<b>The Hill of Golgotha 
The Garden of Gethsemane</b>

00:12:15.610 --> 00:12:20.360
<i>Wait. Do I even know how to 
distinguish quiz bowl difficulty levels?</i>

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:23.530
<i>There have been several questions 
that were pretty obscure,</i>

00:12:23.530 --> 00:12:25.260
<i>but common in quiz bowl terms.</i>

00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:29.020
<i>As for other pilgrimage sites, could it 
be the Church of the Holy Sepulchre?</i>

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:31.150
<i>What others were there?</i>

00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:33.330
<i>How should I answer the question?</i>

00:12:33.330 --> 00:12:34.480
<i>What did Asagaoka have in mind?</i>

00:12:34.910 --> 00:12:36.190
Ten seconds.

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:38.990
<i>Koshiyama looks like he's really struggling.</i>

00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:41.650
<i>I've already settled on my answer.</i>

00:12:41.980 --> 00:12:44.540
<i>The last... That's it!</i>

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:49.020
<i>Maybe it's not about difficulty, but about 
being an appropriate final question for Round 3?</i>

00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:52.100
<i>The genre is Asagaoka's 
specialty: Christianity.</i>

00:12:53.140 --> 00:12:55.830
<i>A Christian pilgrimage site, 
and Jesus Christ's crucifixion...</i>

00:12:55.830 --> 00:13:00.200
<i>His crucifixion? His crucifix? 
His cruci... what?</i>

00:13:00.200 --> 00:13:03.330
<i>Crucifixion... crucifix...</i>

00:13:03.790 --> 00:13:05.840
<i>Appropriate for the last question...</i>

00:13:06.350 --> 00:13:10.210
<i>The last... That's it! The "last"!</i>

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:09.100
World Travel Guide

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:14.720
<i>The last street Christ walked down...</i>

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:17.370
<i>The path walked as he carried the 
crucifix to the hill of Golgotha...</i>

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:19.820
<i>The "Way of Suffering," the Via Dolorosa!</i>

00:13:20.050 --> 00:13:24.320
<i>That's it! The perfect answer to the 
last question of the quarterfinal!</i>

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:33.910
Now, all players, show your boards!

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:35.790
<b>The Church of the Holy Sepulchre</b>

00:13:34.270 --> 00:13:35.790
The Church of the Holy Sepulchre.

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:37.170
Pilate

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:37.170
Pilate.

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:39.040
The Garden of Gethsemane

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:39.040
The Garden of Gethsemane.

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:41.000
<b>Via Dolorosa</b>

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:41.000
Via Dolorosa.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:42.760
Amen

00:13:41.270 --> 00:13:42.210
Amen.

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:45.130
Everyone has given a different answer!

00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:47.130
<i>This answer...</i>

00:13:47.580 --> 00:13:49.140
<i>...will decide the winner!</i>

00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:51.640
Now, let's hear the complete question.

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:54.350
Now a destination for Christian pilgrimages,

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:59.250
Jesus Christ's crucifixion was carried 
out the day after he prayed in a garden,

00:13:57.100 --> 00:14:02.610
Via Dolorosa

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:04.640
where he said, "All who draw the sword 
will die by the sword." Where was this?

00:14:06.350 --> 00:14:07.150
That's...

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:12.790
Round 3, "All Who Draw the Sword Will 
Die by the Sword," will now begin.

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:12.450
<b>Round 3</b>

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:12.450
<b>"All Who Draw the Sword Will 
Die by the Sword" Multiple Answers 
Quiz and Fastest Finger Board Quiz</b>

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:22.380
<b>The Garden of Gethsemane</b>

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:17.180
The correct answer is the 
Garden of Gethsemane.

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:19.620
Since Mikuriya-kun was the 
only one to answer correctly,

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:21.310
he earns two points!

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:24.830
The last to advance from 
the quarterfinal round

00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:26.880
is Miyaura High School 
first-year, Mikuriya-kun!

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:30.390
<b>The Garden of Gethsemane</b>

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:30.390
Congratulations on advancing 
to the semifinal!

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:34.160
<i>The last question was one that 
would only work in this round,</i>

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:36.760
<i>based on the title of the round itself.</i>

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:39.810
<b>Mikuriya</b>

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:41.350
<i>This is the difference between 
Mikuriya-kun's skill and mine.</i>

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:42.610
<b>Koizumi</b>

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:43.320
<b>Koshiyama</b>

00:14:41.740 --> 00:14:42.870
<i>It's a huge difference.</i>

00:14:43.850 --> 00:14:46.540
That concludes Round 3.

00:14:46.540 --> 00:14:48.450
A round of applause 
for all the competitors!

00:14:52.180 --> 00:14:56.420
Mikuriya-kun... I was 
still no match for you.

00:14:56.420 --> 00:14:57.650
I should've known.

00:14:58.090 --> 00:15:01.000
S-Sorry. I thought I was...

00:15:09.240 --> 00:15:09.840
Koshiyama!

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:14.760
What's the Via Dolorosa?

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:19.730
It's the last road that Christ walked down.

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:23.190
It was? I'll remember that.

00:15:24.620 --> 00:15:26.000
You didn't know?

00:15:30.980 --> 00:15:32.110
Revenge!

00:15:32.390 --> 00:15:35.330
I'll take you on as many times as it takes!

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:38.890
Of course, I'm always going to win.

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:43.820
The joys of youth...

00:15:43.820 --> 00:15:45.340
Right, Sonohara?

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:47.510
Is this what you wanted me to see?

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:49.760
If we're done here, I'm leaving.

00:15:57.750 --> 00:15:58.670
Wait!

00:15:58.670 --> 00:15:59.960
Akira!

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:03.650
You're getting punished when we get home!

00:16:04.240 --> 00:16:06.220
Like I care!

00:16:06.970 --> 00:16:07.820
Sonohara!

00:16:09.910 --> 00:16:12.990
We'll still be meeting 
after school every day.

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:15.450
If you feel like it,

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:18.220
come try quiz bowl again.

00:16:23.660 --> 00:16:26.170
Play quiz bowl with us!

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:45.230
I'm sorry, everyone!

00:16:48.240 --> 00:16:52.960
I'm sure some of you were upset by 
our youngest member's behavior.

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:57.070
As our club's president, I will assume 
the responsibility of guiding him.

00:16:57.810 --> 00:16:59.930
I'm responsible, as well.

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:02.460
My brother has caused a 
great deal of trouble.

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:04.160
I'm truly sorry.

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:07.430
Mikuriya, don't you have anything to say?

00:17:07.430 --> 00:17:08.880
You have the right to complain.

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:10.880
His insolent attitude annoys me,

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:13.130
but I have to acknowledge his 
creativity and sheer guts.

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:15.910
I'll beat him next time.

00:17:16.850 --> 00:17:20.060
Koshiyama, he messed with 
you more than anyone else.

00:17:20.060 --> 00:17:22.030
Huh? No, I...

00:17:25.050 --> 00:17:28.520
Seeing what you two are doing 
sort of made me feel relieved.

00:17:29.300 --> 00:17:33.150
I have an upperclassman who apologized 
for me when I messed up, too.

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:36.610
I have friends who want 
to do quiz bowl with me.

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:38.890
And I have people supporting me.

00:17:40.210 --> 00:17:43.650
That hits me really hard, 
and it makes me happy.

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:50.150
So I'm sure he'll understand it, too.

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:51.880
We can't 
clean up 
with you 
people 
there!!

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:53.050
<b>Yeah!</b>

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:53.920
You can 
entrust 
your 
brother 
to me!!

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:53.800
And also, um... 
If you 
don't mind...

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:54.460
He isn't worth 
much, but please 
take care of him!

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:55.050
<b>The older 
sister approves?!</b>

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:58.760
We will now begin to clear the room.

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:04.300
Thank you all for participating in 
the Asagaoka Regular Meet today.

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:08.070
Good work today.

00:18:08.070 --> 00:18:09.410
It was a good meet.

00:18:09.410 --> 00:18:11.730
Our club will have a review 
meeting after this.

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:13.290
Better luck next time.

00:18:13.290 --> 00:18:14.190
You did the best you could.

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:19.370
Today was intense, huh, Koshiyama?

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:21.080
Oh... Yeah.

00:18:21.590 --> 00:18:25.500
<i>The regular meet ended with Sasajima-senpai 
winning by a wide margin.</i>

00:18:27.420 --> 00:18:28.600
That's correct!

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:31.040
<b>Winner</b>

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:31.040
<b>Buzou High School Second-Year 
Sasajima Gakuto-kun</b>

00:18:34.410 --> 00:18:36.760
Congratulations, Sasajima-kun.

00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:38.010
Your thoughts on today?

00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:41.160
This was my first meet in a long time,

00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:43.130
and it was incredibly fun!

00:18:43.860 --> 00:18:49.600
I believe every school here discovered some 
new challenges and goals in this meet.

00:18:50.090 --> 00:18:54.030
I look forward to seeing how everyone 
here performs in the future.

00:18:54.830 --> 00:18:56.810
Now that you've won this meet,

00:18:56.810 --> 00:18:59.200
you'll become a target for 
many other players again.

00:18:59.620 --> 00:19:01.660
A target? Not at all.

00:19:02.730 --> 00:19:04.960
Once a meet ends, we're all equals.

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:07.120
And the next meet will 
be upon us in no time.

00:19:07.570 --> 00:19:09.830
Looks like it's going to be a hot summer.

00:19:10.110 --> 00:19:12.540
It's the last year for us third-years.

00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:14.420
I want to live without regrets.

00:19:17.240 --> 00:19:21.040
Next time, just like today, we'll all 
start from the same starting line.

00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:24.850
I look forward to competing 
with you all again.

00:19:26.110 --> 00:19:29.140
I wanted to keep going...

00:19:29.410 --> 00:19:32.120
Ya just gotta try your hardest next time!

00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:35.070
Players from all over the country 
will be at the next meet.

00:19:35.420 --> 00:19:37.610
They'll all be aiming for victory.

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:40.570
The High School Quiz Bowl Championship, huh?

00:19:41.100 --> 00:19:42.820
From all over the country?

00:19:43.370 --> 00:19:45.670
Even more veteran players we 
haven't met will be there!

00:19:46.610 --> 00:19:48.740
This really feels like being 
in a club, doesn't it?!

00:19:49.350 --> 00:19:50.580
I've never felt this before!

00:19:51.110 --> 00:19:52.040
Y-Yeah!

00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:56.550
Fukami-san, thanks for inviting 
me to the quiz circle.

00:19:58.220 --> 00:20:00.630
Let's all take on more challenges together.

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:37.980
Mikuriya-kun!

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:43.200
Thanks for today!

00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:45.140
I'll be looking forward to next time!

00:21:45.140 --> 00:21:45.900
Then, I'll—

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:48.120
Will beating me satisfy you?

00:21:49.620 --> 00:21:51.440
There's always someone better.

00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:53.480
If you drag your feet, 
you'll never catch up.

00:21:53.480 --> 00:21:55.290
I won't wait for you.

00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:04.460
I only acknowledge people 
who are aiming higher!

00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:08.600
<i>I've found an incredible rival.</i>

00:22:15.120 --> 00:22:17.790
<i>You really are ruthless.</i>

00:22:19.650 --> 00:22:22.680
<i>And what lies ahead of where my 
incredible rival is trying to go...</i>

00:22:22.680 --> 00:22:25.670
<i>I want to see what's there, too!</i>

00:22:36.440 --> 00:22:37.520
I will aim higher.

00:22:42.830 --> 00:22:45.670
It's a contest to see which 
of us can make it higher!
